{
  "$comment": "The format metadata for every language magical_rs ships in.\n\nThis file is the source of truth. Two scripts read it and nothing else writes\nany of these values:\n\n  scripts/gen_kinds.ps1       crates/magical_rs/src/magical/kinds_meta.rs\n                              bindings/python/python/magical_py/_kinds.py\n  scripts/gen_formats.mjs    bindings/nodejs/_kinds.js\n                              bindings/nodejs/_kinds.d.ts\n\nEvery field here is read by at least one of them and by at least one test. A\nfield nothing reads is worse than no field: it is a second answer waiting to\ndisagree, and the magic bytes would have been the obvious one to add. They are\nin readme.md instead, because they are facts about the formats rather than\nmetadata about this project's table, and readme_coverage.rs checks them against\nSIGNATURE_KIND -- the code that matches on them.\n\nFields:\n  variant    the Rust enum member, in src/magical/magic.rs\n  abi_order  its position in that enum. This is the ABI: a kind crosses the wasm\n            boundary as its discriminant, so entry N here is what the compiled\n            module reports as N. Read it out of the declaration; do not renumber.\n  token      a short stable identifier, such as \"psd\" or \"bz2\". The Python enum\n            member value, and what a catalogue sorts by. Not the same as\n            `extension`: Png is \"png\" either way, but Lua is \"luac\" here\n            because a .lua file is source and this table detects byte code.\n  name       the display name, as documentation and a catalogue write it\n  mime       the registered MIME type, or null. Null means \"not registered\",\n            never \"unknown\" -- a wrong MIME type is served to a browser.\n  extension  the conventional extension without a dot, or null. Advisory: detection\n            never reads a file name.\n\nThe count is 114 and every generated file and every test states it.",
